# =============================================================================
# hetero-backward — G3 heterogeneous-output fixture (gpu-training stage-3r)
# =============================================================================
#
# What this proves (G3):
#   • An AIR-generated backward fixture whose gradient tuple has genuinely
#     unequal output extents — grad_x: tf32[4] and grad_w: tf32[2] — executes
#     safely on Metal and CUDA. Each output receives exactly its declared
#     element count, with per-output dispatch extent and bounds (R6/P1); no
#     shared extent overruns the smaller buffer or leaves the larger one
#     partial.
#   • Both outputs match an independent analytic oracle under
#     numeric-policy v1.0.0 (reduction-sum row; values are exactly
#     representable, so the policy floor is a backstop, not a rounding claim).
#
# The workload: loss = sum(x) with x: tf32[4]. The function signature also
# selects a second parameter w: tf32[2] which is unused in the body, so the
# AIR-generated companion `hetero_backward` returns a genuinely heterogeneous
# tuple:
#   forward  sx = sum(x) = 10.0
#   backward grad_x[i] = upstream = 1.0  (4 elements)
#           grad_w[j] = 0.0              (2 elements — d loss/d w = 0)
#
# Why this shape: the current device substrate combines different-shaped
# parameters only through broadcast or matmul, and the elementwise device
# kernel ABI accepts only same-element-count kernels; an unused selected
# parameter is the source-expressible route to a second, smaller gradient
# extent. The mathematical values are exact; the G3 substance is the
# heterogeneous output BOUNDS on real devices (the [2] buffer must never be
# overrun by the union [4] dispatch, and the [4] buffer must never be left
# partial).
#
# This file is READ-ONLY: it is the pinned oracle input (S2-5 convention).
# The host input values live in faber.toml `[device] inputs`; the CPU
# reference is pinned in oracle/ under numeric-policy v1.0.0.
#
# See also: examples/training/mul-mean (S3-B1 fixture convention),
# examples/training/device-summa-recollige (S2-5 fixture convention),
# crates/radix-mir-llvm/tests/device_mode.rs + crates/radix-mir-metal
# (U3 heterogeneous multi-output emitter proofs, [4]/[2] MIR fixtures).
# =============================================================================

# nil() — vacuum residual for the companion backward ABI.
functio nil() → vacuum {
    tacet
}

@ nucleum
@ radix lane "air"
@ radix backward "hetero_backward"
functio hetero_loss(tf32[4] x, tf32[2] w) → f32 {
    fixum f32 sx ← x.sum()
    redde sx
}
